/-!
# `p`-linear endomorphisms of vector spaces in characteristic `p`

Let `k` be a field of characteristic `p > 0` and `V` a `k`-vector space. A *`p`-linear*
endomorphism of `V` is a semilinear map `F : V →ₛₗ[frobenius k p] V`, that is, an additive map
with `F (a • v) = a ^ p • F v`. Its fixed points form an `𝔽_p`-subspace of `V`, recorded here
as the additive subgroup `LinearMap.Frobenius.fixedPoints F`.

Throughout, `V →ₚ[k, p] W` is local notation for `V →ₛₗ[frobenius k p] W`.

Three basic facts are stated: the fixed points are finite with at most `p ^ dim V` elements;
over an algebraically closed field `v ↦ F v - v` is surjective (Lang–Steinberg); and the fixed
points do not change under an extension of algebraically closed fields.

## Main definitions

- `LinearMap.Frobenius.fixedPoints`: the additive subgroup of fixed points of a `p`-linear map.
- `LinearMap.Frobenius.fixedPointsSubmodule`: the fixed points as a subspace over the prime
  subfield of `k`.

## Main statements

- `LinearMap.Frobenius.finite_fixedPoints`, `LinearMap.Frobenius.natCard_fixedPoints_le`:
  the fixed points are finite, of cardinality at most `p ^ Module.finrank k V`.
- `LinearMap.Frobenius.surjective_sub_id`: Lang–Steinberg for `p`-linear maps.
- `LinearMap.Frobenius.exists_submodule_sub_id_surjOn`: every nonzero vector lies in an
  `F`-stable subspace on which `F - 1` is surjective.
- `LinearMap.Frobenius.existsUnique_baseChange`: a `p`-linear endomorphism has a unique
  `p`-linear base change to `k' ⊗[k] V`.
- `LinearMap.Frobenius.bijective_tmul_fixedPoints`: the fixed points are unchanged by an
  algebraically closed base change.

## Implementation notes

The proof of Lang–Steinberg avoids the structure theorem for modules over the skew polynomial
ring `k[τ]` used in blueprint `lem-sc-lang-steinberg`. Instead, it inducts on `dim V`: the cyclic
subspace `W` generated by a nonzero vector is `F`-stable, `F - 1` is surjective on `W` by the
explicit block computation of the blueprint (`exists_sub_id_eq_of_iterate_eq`), and `F - 1` is
surjective on `V ⧸ W` by induction. Surjectivity on `W` and on `V ⧸ W` gives surjectivity on `V`.

Rather than equipping the fixed points with a `Module (ZMod p)` structure — which is not
available by instance search for a bare `k`-vector space — the dimension bound of
`sk-prop-av-fixed-points` is stated in the equivalent cardinality form
`Nat.card (fixedPoints F) ≤ p ^ Module.finrank k V`.

The `𝔽_p`-structure on the fixed points is realised by the prime subfield `⊥ : Subfield k`,
whose elements are exactly the `x` with `x ^ p = x`: the fixed points form the
`⊥`-submodule `LinearMap.Frobenius.fixedPointsSubmodule F` of `V`. The key step
`LinearMap.Frobenius.linearIndependent_of_mem_fixedPoints` shows that `⊥`-linearly independent
fixed points are `k`-linearly independent, which bounds the `⊥`-dimension by `dim_k V`.

The base change of `sk-prop-av-fixed-base-change` is written as `k' ⊗[k] V` (rather than
`V ⊗[k] k'`), since that is the side on which Mathlib provides the `k'`-module structure. The
base-changed map `F'` is taken as a hypothesis rather than constructed;
`LinearMap.Frobenius.existsUnique_baseChange` records that exactly one such map exists, so that
the hypothesis is not vacuous.

The proof of `bijective_tmul_fixedPoints` does not use the cyclic-block normal form of the
blueprint. Writing a fixed point of `F'` as `∑ cᵢ ⊗ eᵢ` in a `k`-basis `e` of `V`, the
coordinates satisfy `cⱼ = ∑ᵢ aⱼᵢ cᵢ ^ p` with `aⱼᵢ ∈ k`. A dimension count shows that the `k`-span
of the `cᵢ` in `k'` is stable under `x ↦ x ^ p`, so each `cᵢ` is algebraic over `k`, hence lies
in `k` since `k` is algebraically closed.
-/

@[expose] public section

open scoped TensorProduct

section Auxiliary

open Polynomial

variable {k K : Type*} {p : ℕ} [Field k] [Fact p.Prime] [Field K] [Algebra k K]

/-- An element whose iterated `p`-th powers stay in a finite-dimensional subspace is algebraic. -/
private theorem isAlgebraic_of_pow_pow_mem (W : Submodule k K) [FiniteDimensional k W] {x : K}
    (hx : ∀ i : ℕ, x ^ p ^ i ∈ W) : IsAlgebraic k x := by
  by_contra h
  set d := Module.finrank k W
  have hli : LinearIndependent k (fun i : Fin (d + 1) ↦ (⟨x ^ p ^ (i : ℕ), hx i⟩ : W)) := by
    refine LinearIndependent.of_comp W.subtype ?_
    rw [Fintype.linearIndependent_iff]
    intro g hg i
    have hq : aeval x (∑ j : Fin (d + 1), C (g j) * X ^ p ^ (j : ℕ)) = 0 := by
      simpa [Algebra.smul_def] using hg
    have h0 := (transcendental_iff.mp h) _ hq
    have := congrArg (coeff · (p ^ (i : ℕ))) h0
    simp only [finsetSum_coeff, coeff_C_mul_X_pow, coeff_zero] at this
    rwa [Finset.sum_eq_single i (fun j _ hj ↦ by
        rw [if_neg]; exact fun e ↦ hj (Fin.ext
          (Nat.pow_right_injective (Fact.out : p.Prime).two_le e).symm))
      (by simp), if_pos rfl] at this
  simpa [d] using hli.fintype_card_le_finrank

/-- Over an algebraically closed field `k`, every element algebraic over `k` lies in `k`. -/
private theorem mem_range_algebraMap_of_isAlgebraic [IsAlgClosed k] {x : K} (hx : IsAlgebraic k x) :
    x ∈ (algebraMap k K).range := by
  have hi := hx.isIntegral
  exact minpoly.mem_range_of_degree_eq_one k x
    (IsAlgClosed.degree_eq_one_of_irreducible k (minpoly.irreducible hi))

/-- If every member of a finite family `c` in a field of characteristic `p` is a `k`-linear
combination of the `p`-th powers `c i ^ p`, then the `k`-span `W` of the family is stable under
`x ↦ x ^ p`: indeed `W` lies in the span of the `p`-th powers of a basis of `W`, which has
dimension at most `dim W`. Hence all iterated powers `c j ^ p ^ m` lie in `W`. -/
private theorem pow_pow_mem_span_of_mem_span_pow [CharP K p] {ι : Type*} [Finite ι] {c : ι → K}
    (hc : ∀ j, c j ∈ Submodule.span k (Set.range fun i ↦ c i ^ p)) (j : ι) (m : ℕ) :
    c j ^ p ^ m ∈ Submodule.span k (Set.range c) := by
  set W := Submodule.span k (Set.range c)
  have : FiniteDimensional k W := FiniteDimensional.span_of_finite k (Set.finite_range c)
  set b := Module.finBasis k W
  set U := Submodule.span k (Set.range fun l ↦ (b l : K) ^ p)
  have : FiniteDimensional k U := FiniteDimensional.span_of_finite k (Set.finite_range _)
  have hpow : ∀ x ∈ W, x ^ p ∈ U := by
    intro x hx
    rw [← show ((⟨x, hx⟩ : W) : K) = x from rfl, ← b.sum_repr ⟨x, hx⟩]
    simp only [Submodule.coe_sum, Submodule.coe_smul, Algebra.smul_def]
    rw [sum_pow_char]
    refine Submodule.sum_mem _ fun l _ ↦ ?_
    rw [mul_pow, ← map_pow, ← Algebra.smul_def]
    exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (Submodule.subset_span ⟨l, rfl⟩)
  have hWU : W ≤ U := Submodule.span_le.mpr <| by
    rintro _ ⟨j, rfl⟩
    refine Submodule.span_le.mpr ?_ (hc j)
    rintro _ ⟨i, rfl⟩
    exact hpow _ (Submodule.subset_span ⟨i, rfl⟩)
  have hUW : W = U := Submodule.eq_of_le_of_finrank_le hWU <|
    (finrank_range_le_card _).trans (by simp [W])
  induction m with
  | zero => simpa using (Submodule.subset_span (Set.mem_range_self j) : c j ∈ W)
  | succ m ih => rw [pow_succ, pow_mul]; exact hUW ▸ hpow _ ih

end Auxiliary

namespace LinearMap

namespace Frobenius

/-- `V →ₚ[k, p] W` is the type of `p`-linear (that is, `frobenius k p`-semilinear) maps. -/
local notation:25 V " →ₚ[" k ", " p "] " W => LinearMap (_root_.frobenius k p) V W

variable {k V : Type*} {p : ℕ} [Field k] [Fact p.Prime] [CharP k p] [AddCommGroup V]
  [Module k V]

/-- The additive subgroup of fixed points of a `p`-linear endomorphism `F` of `V`. It is in fact
an `𝔽_p`-subspace, since `F` is additive and fixes the prime field. -/
def fixedPoints (F : V →ₚ[k, p] V) : AddSubgroup V where
  carrier := {v | F v = v}
  zero_mem' := map_zero F
  add_mem' {a b} ha hb := show F (a + b) = a + b by rw [map_add, ha, hb]
  neg_mem' {a} ha := show F (-a) = -a by rw [map_neg, ha]

@[simp]
theorem mem_fixedPoints {F : V →ₚ[k, p] V} {v : V} : v ∈ fixedPoints F ↔ F v = v :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- The fixed points of a `p`-linear endomorphism `F` of `V`, as a subspace over the prime subfield
`⊥ : Subfield k` (that is, over `𝔽_p`). Its underlying additive subgroup is `fixedPoints F`. -/
def fixedPointsSubmodule (F : V →ₚ[k, p] V) : Submodule (⊥ : Subfield k) V where
  toAddSubmonoid := (fixedPoints F).toAddSubmonoid
  smul_mem' a v hv := by
    change F (a • v) = a • v
    rw [Subfield.smul_def, map_smulₛₗ, _root_.frobenius_def,
      (Subfield.mem_bot_iff_pow_eq_self k p).mp a.2, mem_fixedPoints.mp hv]

@[simp]
theorem mem_fixedPointsSubmodule {F : V →ₚ[k, p] V} {v : V} :
    v ∈ fixedPointsSubmodule F ↔ F v = v :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- The fixed points as an additive subgroup and as a submodule over the prime subfield have the
same elements. -/
def fixedPointsEquivSubmodule (F : V →ₚ[k, p] V) : fixedPoints F ≃ fixedPointsSubmodule F :=
  Equiv.subtypeEquivRight fun _ ↦ Iff.rfl

/-- Key step of blueprint `lem-sc-fixed-points-finite`: a finite family of fixed points of a
`p`-linear map which is linearly independent over the prime subfield `𝔽_p` is linearly
independent over `k`.

Given a `k`-linear dependence `∑ gᵢ vᵢ = 0` of minimal support, normalise it so that `g i₀ = 1`;
applying `F` gives `∑ gᵢ ^ p vᵢ = 0`, and subtracting yields the shorter dependence
`∑ (gᵢ - gᵢ ^ p) vᵢ = 0`. By minimality `gᵢ ^ p = gᵢ`, so all `gᵢ` lie in `𝔽_p`, contradicting
`𝔽_p`-independence. -/
theorem linearIndependent_of_mem_fixedPoints (F : V →ₚ[k, p] V) {ι : Type*} [Finite ι]
    {v : ι → V} (hv : ∀ i, v i ∈ fixedPoints F)
    (hli : LinearIndependent (⊥ : Subfield k) v) : LinearIndependent k v := by
  classical
  cases nonempty_fintype ι
  rw [Fintype.linearIndependent_iff]
  suffices H : ∀ n : ℕ, ∀ g : ι → k, (Finset.univ.filter (g · ≠ 0)).card ≤ n →
      ∑ i, g i • v i = 0 → g = 0 from fun g hg ↦ congrFun (H _ g le_rfl hg)
  intro n
  induction n with
  | zero =>
    intro g hcard _
    ext i
    by_contra hi
    simp only [Nat.le_zero, Finset.card_eq_zero, Finset.filter_eq_empty_iff, Finset.mem_univ,
      true_implies, not_not] at hcard
    exact hi (@hcard i)
  | succ n ih =>
    intro g hcard hg
    by_contra hne
    obtain ⟨i₀, hi₀⟩ := Function.ne_iff.mp hne
    set h : ι → k := fun i ↦ (g i₀)⁻¹ * g i with hh
    have hh₀ : h i₀ = 1 := inv_mul_cancel₀ hi₀
    have hsum : ∑ i, h i • v i = 0 := by
      simp_rw [hh, mul_smul, ← Finset.smul_sum, hg, smul_zero]
    have hsumF : ∑ i, h i ^ p • v i = 0 := by
      have := congrArg F hsum
      simpa [map_sum, map_smulₛₗ, _root_.frobenius_def, mem_fixedPoints.mp (hv _)] using this
    have hdiff : (fun i ↦ h i - h i ^ p) = 0 := by
      refine ih _ ?_ (by simp_rw [sub_smul, Finset.sum_sub_distrib, hsum, hsumF, sub_zero])
      have hsub : Finset.univ.filter (fun i ↦ h i - h i ^ p ≠ 0) ⊆
          (Finset.univ.filter (g · ≠ 0)).erase i₀ := by
        intro i hi
        simp only [Finset.mem_filter, Finset.mem_univ, true_and, Finset.mem_erase] at hi ⊢
        refine ⟨fun e ↦ hi (by simp [e, hh₀]), fun e ↦ hi ?_⟩
        simp [hh, e, zero_pow (Fact.out : p.Prime).ne_zero]
      have := Finset.card_le_card hsub
      rw [Finset.card_erase_of_mem (by simpa using hi₀)] at this
      omega
    have hbot : ∀ i, h i ∈ (⊥ : Subfield k) := fun i ↦
      (Subfield.mem_bot_iff_pow_eq_self k p).mpr (sub_eq_zero.mp (congrFun hdiff i)).symm
    have := Fintype.linearIndependent_iff.mp hli (fun i ↦ ⟨h i, hbot i⟩) hsum i₀
    simp [Subtype.ext_iff, hh₀] at this

/-- The fixed points of `F` have rank at most `dim_k V` over the prime subfield. -/
theorem rank_fixedPointsSubmodule_le [FiniteDimensional k V] (F : V →ₚ[k, p] V) :
    Module.rank (⊥ : Subfield k) (fixedPointsSubmodule F) ≤ Module.finrank k V := by
  refine _root_.rank_le fun s hs ↦ ?_
  have := (linearIndependent_of_mem_fixedPoints F (v := fun i : s ↦ ((i : _) : V))
    (fun i ↦ (i : fixedPointsSubmodule F).2) (hs.map' _ (Submodule.ker_subtype _)))
  simpa using this.fintype_card_le_finrank

/-- The fixed points of `F` are finite-dimensional over the prime subfield. -/
instance finite_fixedPointsSubmodule [FiniteDimensional k V] (F : V →ₚ[k, p] V) :
    Module.Finite (⊥ : Subfield k) (fixedPointsSubmodule F) :=
  Module.rank_lt_aleph0_iff.mp <|
    (rank_fixedPointsSubmodule_le F).trans_lt Cardinal.natCast_lt_aleph0

/-- The fixed points of `F` have dimension at most `dim_k V` over the prime subfield. -/
theorem finrank_fixedPointsSubmodule_le [FiniteDimensional k V] (F : V →ₚ[k, p] V) :
    Module.finrank (⊥ : Subfield k) (fixedPointsSubmodule F) ≤ Module.finrank k V :=
  Module.finrank_le_of_rank_le (rank_fixedPointsSubmodule_le F)

/-- Blueprint `sk-prop-av-fixed-points`: Fixed points of `p`-linear maps are finite.

Let `k` be a field of characteristic `p > 0`, let `V` be a finite-dimensional `k`-vector space
and let `F : V →ₛₗ[frobenius k p] V` be `p`-linear. Then the fixed points of `F` form a finite
`𝔽_p`-subspace of `V`. This is the finiteness part of blueprint `lem-sc-fixed-points-finite`. -/
instance finite_fixedPoints [FiniteDimensional k V] (F : V →ₚ[k, p] V) :
    Finite (fixedPoints F) :=
  have : Finite (⊥ : Subfield k) :=
    Nat.finite_of_card_ne_zero ((Subfield.card_bot k p).trans_ne (Fact.out : p.Prime).ne_zero)
  have := Module.finite_of_finite (⊥ : Subfield k) (M := fixedPointsSubmodule F)
  .of_equiv _ (fixedPointsEquivSubmodule F).symm

/-- Blueprint `sk-prop-av-fixed-points`: Fixed points of `p`-linear maps are finite.

The `𝔽_p`-subspace of fixed points of a `p`-linear endomorphism `F` of a finite-dimensional
`k`-vector space `V` has `𝔽_p`-dimension at most `Module.finrank k V`; equivalently, it has at
most `p ^ Module.finrank k V` elements. This is the dimension bound of blueprint
`lem-sc-fixed-points-finite`. -/
theorem natCard_fixedPoints_le [FiniteDimensional k V] (F : V →ₚ[k, p] V) :
    Nat.card (fixedPoints F) ≤ p ^ Module.finrank k V := by
  rw [Nat.card_congr (fixedPointsEquivSubmodule F),
    Module.natCard_eq_pow_finrank (K := (⊥ : Subfield k)), Subfield.card_bot k p]
  exact Nat.pow_le_pow_right (Fact.out : p.Prime).pos (finrank_fixedPointsSubmodule_le F)

open Polynomial in
/-- Step 3 of blueprint `lem-sc-lang-steinberg`, solving on a cyclic block. Let `F` be
`p`-linear over an algebraically closed field and let `v` satisfy the relation
`F^[m] v = ∑_{i < m} aᵢ • F^[i] v`. Then every `w = ∑_{i < m} cᵢ • F^[i] v` is of the form
`F x - x` for some `x = ∑_{i < m} xᵢ • F^[i] v`.

The coordinates are found by back-substitution: with `P₀ = 0` and
`P_{i+1} = P_i ^ p + aᵢ X ^ p - cᵢ`, put `xᵢ = P_{i+1}(y)`, where `y` is a root of `P_m - X`.
Such a root exists because `P_m` has vanishing derivative, so `P_m - X` is not constant. The
linear independence of the `F^[i] v` is not needed. -/
theorem exists_sub_id_eq_of_iterate_eq [IsAlgClosed k] (F : V →ₚ[k, p] V) (v : V) {m : ℕ}
    (a c : ℕ → k) (ha : F^[m] v = ∑ i ∈ Finset.range m, a i • F^[i] v) :
    ∃ x : ℕ → k, F (∑ i ∈ Finset.range m, x i • F^[i] v) - ∑ i ∈ Finset.range m, x i • F^[i] v =
      ∑ i ∈ Finset.range m, c i • F^[i] v := by
  let P : ℕ → k[X] := fun n ↦ Nat.rec 0 (fun i Q ↦ Q ^ p + C (a i) * X ^ p - C (c i)) n
  have hP0 : P 0 = 0 := rfl
  have hPs (i : ℕ) : P (i + 1) = P i ^ p + C (a i) * X ^ p - C (c i) := rfl
  clear_value P
  have hd (i : ℕ) : derivative (P i) = 0 := by
    induction i with
    | zero => simp [hP0]
    | succ i ih => simp [hPs, ih, derivative_pow, CharP.cast_eq_zero]
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := IsAlgClosed.exists_eval_sub_self_eq_of_derivative_eq_zero (hd m) 0
  rw [sub_eq_zero] at hy
  refine ⟨fun i ↦ (P (i + 1)).eval y, ?_⟩
  have hF : F (∑ i ∈ Finset.range m, (P (i + 1)).eval y • F^[i] v) =
      ∑ i ∈ Finset.range m, (((P i).eval y) ^ p + a i * y ^ p) • F^[i] v := by
    simp only [map_sum, map_smulₛₗ, _root_.frobenius_def, ← Function.iterate_succ_apply' F]
    rw [show ∑ i ∈ Finset.range m, (P (i + 1)).eval y ^ p • F^[i.succ] v =
        ∑ i ∈ Finset.range (m + 1), (P i).eval y ^ p • F^[i] v by
      simp [Finset.sum_range_succ' _ m, hP0, (Fact.out : p.Prime).ne_zero],
      Finset.sum_range_succ, ha, hy, Finset.smul_sum, ← Finset.sum_add_distrib]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ ↦ ?_
    rw [smul_smul, ← add_smul, mul_comm]
  rw [hF, ← Finset.sum_sub_distrib]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ ↦ ?_
  beta_reduce
  rw [← sub_smul, hPs]
  congr 1
  simp only [eval_sub, eval_add, eval_pow, eval_mul, eval_C, eval_X]
  ring

/-- Steps 1–3 of blueprint `lem-sc-lang-steinberg`: every nonzero vector `v` lies in an
`F`-stable subspace `W` on which `x ↦ F x - x` is surjective, namely the cyclic subspace spanned by
`v, F v, F^[2] v, …`. -/
theorem exists_submodule_sub_id_surjOn [IsAlgClosed k] [FiniteDimensional k V]
    (F : V →ₚ[k, p] V) {v : V} (hv : v ≠ 0) :
    ∃ W : Submodule k V, W ≤ W.comap F ∧ W ≠ ⊥ ∧ ∀ w ∈ W, ∃ x ∈ W, F x - x = w := by
  let S : ℕ →o Submodule k V :=
    ⟨fun n ↦ Submodule.span k ((F^[·] v) '' Set.Iio n), fun _ _ h ↦
      Submodule.span_mono (Set.image_mono (Set.Iio_subset_Iio h))⟩
  have hS {n : ℕ} {w : V} : w ∈ S n ↔ ∃ c : ℕ → k, ∑ i ∈ Finset.range n, c i • F^[i] v = w := by
    refine ⟨fun hw ↦ ?_, ?_⟩
    · obtain ⟨l, hl, rfl⟩ := Finsupp.mem_span_image_iff_linearCombination k |>.mp hw
      exact ⟨l, (Finsupp.linearCombination_apply_of_mem_supported k
        (s := Finset.range n) (by simpa using hl)).symm⟩
    · rintro ⟨c, rfl⟩
      exact Submodule.sum_mem _ fun i hi ↦ Submodule.smul_mem _ _
        (Submodule.subset_span ⟨i, by simpa using hi, rfl⟩)
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := monotone_stabilizes_iff_noetherian.mpr inferInstance S
  have hsucc : S (n + 1) = S n := (hn _ n.le_succ).symm
  have hgen {i : ℕ} (hi : i ≤ n) : F^[i] v ∈ S n := by
    rw [← hsucc]
    exact Submodule.subset_span ⟨i, Nat.lt_succ_of_le hi, rfl⟩
  refine ⟨S n, fun x hx ↦ ?_, ?_, fun w hw ↦ ?_⟩
  · obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ := hS.mp hx
    simp only [Submodule.mem_comap, map_sum, map_smulₛₗ, ← Function.iterate_succ_apply' F]
    exact Submodule.sum_mem _ fun i hi ↦ Submodule.smul_mem _ _
      (hgen (Finset.mem_range.mp hi))
  · exact fun h ↦ hv (by simpa [h] using hgen (Nat.zero_le n))
  · obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := hS.mp (hgen le_rfl)
    obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ := hS.mp hw
    obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := exists_sub_id_eq_of_iterate_eq F v a c ha.symm
    exact ⟨_, hS.mpr ⟨x, rfl⟩, hx⟩

/-- Blueprint `sk-prop-av-lang-steinberg`: Lang–Steinberg for `p`-linear maps.

Let `k` be an algebraically closed field of characteristic `p > 0`, let `V` be a
finite-dimensional `k`-vector space and let `F : V →ₛₗ[frobenius k p] V` be `p`-linear. Then
`v ↦ F v - v` is surjective. -/
theorem surjective_sub_id [IsAlgClosed k] [FiniteDimensional k V] (F : V →ₚ[k, p] V) :
    Function.Surjective fun v ↦ F v - v := by
  induction hn : Module.finrank k V using Nat.strong_induction_on generalizing V with
  | _ n ih =>
  intro w
  rcases subsingleton_or_nontrivial V with hV | hV
  · exact ⟨0, Subsingleton.elim _ _⟩
  obtain ⟨v, hv⟩ := exists_ne (0 : V)
  obtain ⟨W, hWF, hW, hWs⟩ := exists_submodule_sub_id_surjOn F hv
  have hlt : Module.finrank k (V ⧸ W) < n := by
    have := W.finrank_quotient_add_finrank
    have := (Module.finrank_pos_iff (R := k)).mpr (Submodule.nontrivial_iff_ne_bot.mpr hW)
    omega
  obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := ih _ hlt (W.mapQ W F hWF) rfl (W.mkQ w)
  obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := W.mkQ_surjective x
  have hmem : F x - x - w ∈ W := by
    rw [← Submodule.Quotient.eq]
    simpa using hx
  obtain ⟨u, -, hu⟩ := hWs _ hmem
  refine ⟨x - u, ?_⟩
  simp only [map_sub]
  rw [show F x - F u - (x - u) = (F x - x) - (F u - u) by abel, hu]
  abel

variable {k' : Type*} [Field k'] [CharP k' p] [Algebra k k']

/-- A `p`-linear endomorphism `F` of `V` has exactly one `p`-linear extension to the base change
`k' ⊗[k] V`, namely `a ⊗ₜ v ↦ a ^ p ⊗ₜ F v`. This is the map `F' = F ⊗ σ_{k'}` of blueprint
`sk-prop-av-fixed-base-change`. -/
theorem existsUnique_baseChange (F : V →ₚ[k, p] V) :
    ∃! F' : (k' ⊗[k] V) →ₚ[k', p] (k' ⊗[k] V), ∀ v : V, F' (1 ⊗ₜ[k] v) = 1 ⊗ₜ[k] F v := by
  let f : k' →+ V →+ k' ⊗[k] V :=
    { toFun a := (TensorProduct.mk k k' V (a ^ p)).toAddMonoidHom.comp F.toAddMonoidHom
      map_zero' := by ext; simp [zero_pow (Fact.out : p.Prime).ne_zero]
      map_add' a b := by ext; simp [add_pow_char] }
  let G := TensorProduct.liftAddHom f fun (r : k) a v ↦ by
    change ((r • a) ^ p) ⊗ₜ[k] F v = (a ^ p) ⊗ₜ[k] F (r • v)
    rw [map_smulₛₗ, _root_.frobenius_def, TensorProduct.tmul_smul, TensorProduct.smul_tmul',
      smul_pow]
  have hG (a : k') (v : V) : G (a ⊗ₜ[k] v) = (a ^ p) ⊗ₜ[k] F v := rfl
  refine ⟨{ toFun := G, map_add' := G.map_add, map_smul' := fun c x ↦ ?_ }, fun v ↦ ?_,
    fun F'' hF'' ↦ ?_⟩
  · induction x using TensorProduct.induction_on with
    | zero => simp
    | tmul a v => simp [TensorProduct.smul_tmul', hG, mul_pow, _root_.frobenius_def]
    | add x y hx hy => simp only [smul_add, map_add] at hx hy ⊢; rw [hx, hy]
  · simp [hG]
  · ext x
    induction x using TensorProduct.induction_on with
    | zero => simp
    | tmul a v =>
      rw [show a ⊗ₜ[k] v = a • (1 ⊗ₜ[k] v) by simp [TensorProduct.smul_tmul'], map_smulₛₗ,
        hF'']
      simp [hG, TensorProduct.smul_tmul', _root_.frobenius_def]
    | add x y hx hy => simp only [map_add, hx, hy]

/-- Blueprint `sk-prop-av-fixed-base-change` (proved as `lem-sc-frobenius-fixed-invariance`):
Fixed points are unchanged by algebraically closed base change.

Let `k ⊆ k'` be an extension of algebraically closed fields of characteristic `p > 0`, let `V`
be a finite-dimensional `k`-vector space and let `F : V →ₛₗ[frobenius k p] V` be `p`-linear. If
`F'` is a `p`-linear endomorphism of the base change `k' ⊗[k] V` with `F' (1 ⊗ₜ v) = 1 ⊗ₜ F v`
for all `v` — that is, the base change of `F` of `existsUnique_baseChange` — then `v ↦ 1 ⊗ₜ v`
is a bijection from the fixed points of `F` onto the fixed points of `F'`. -/
theorem bijective_tmul_fixedPoints [IsAlgClosed k] [IsAlgClosed k'] [FiniteDimensional k V]
    (F : V →ₚ[k, p] V) (F' : (k' ⊗[k] V) →ₚ[k', p] (k' ⊗[k] V))
    (hF' : ∀ v : V, F' (1 ⊗ₜ[k] v) = 1 ⊗ₜ[k] F v) :
    Function.Bijective fun v : fixedPoints F ↦
      (⟨1 ⊗ₜ[k] (v : V), by rw [mem_fixedPoints, hF', mem_fixedPoints.mp v.2]⟩ :
        fixedPoints F') := by
  set b := Module.finBasis k V
  set B := Algebra.TensorProduct.basis k' b
  have hinj : Function.Injective fun v : V ↦ (1 : k') ⊗ₜ[k] v := by
    intro u v huv
    refine b.repr.injective (Finsupp.ext fun i ↦ (algebraMap k k').injective ?_)
    simpa [B] using congrArg (fun w ↦ B.repr w i) huv
  refine ⟨fun u v huv ↦ Subtype.ext (hinj (congrArg Subtype.val huv)), fun w ↦ ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ : ∃ c : _ → k', ⇑(B.repr w) = c := ⟨_, rfl⟩
  have key (j) : c j = ∑ i, b.repr (F (b i)) j • c i ^ p := by
    rw [← hc]
    conv_lhs => rw [← mem_fixedPoints.mp w.2, ← B.sum_repr w]
    simp [B, map_sum, hF', Algebra.smul_def, mul_comm]
    rfl
  have := FiniteDimensional.span_of_finite k (Set.finite_range c)
  have hd (j) : c j ∈ (algebraMap k k').range := by
    refine mem_range_algebraMap_of_isAlgebraic (isAlgebraic_of_pow_pow_mem (p := p)
      (Submodule.span k (Set.range c)) (pow_pow_mem_span_of_mem_span_pow (fun j ↦ ?_) j))
    rw [key j]
    exact Submodule.sum_mem _ fun i _ ↦ Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (Submodule.subset_span ⟨i, rfl⟩)
  choose d hd using hd
  set v := ∑ j, d j • b j
  have hv : (1 : k') ⊗ₜ[k] v = w := B.repr.injective <| Finsupp.ext fun j ↦ by
    simp [v, B, map_sum, Finsupp.single_apply, hd, ← hc]
  refine ⟨⟨v, hinj ?_⟩, Subtype.ext hv⟩
  change (1 : k') ⊗ₜ[k] F v = 1 ⊗ₜ[k] v
  rw [← hF', hv, mem_fixedPoints.mp w.2]

end Frobenius

end LinearMap
